+/*
+ * miami (Motorola Edge 30 Neo, SM6375): Adreno 619 (GMU-wrapper "holi", chipid 0x6010901) bring-up.
+ *
+ * Moved out of sweet_touch_gt9916.c. Boot-args:
+ *   sweetgpu=1       power up the GPU, authenticate the zap shader, start the CP and run the CP_MEM_WRITE self test
+ *   sweetgpu=2       the same, then run the A2D blit demo (a gradient square drawn on the panel, 300 frames)
+ *   sweetgpudebug=1  verbose log: print every register access and pause 100-1500 ms around the risky ones, so the
+ *                    last log line names the culprit if the phone hangs. Without it the run is quiet and fast.
+ *   sweetgpuprobe=16/17 are accepted as aliases for sweetgpu=1/2 (the old probe stages 1-15 are gone).
+ *
+ * Sequence (all proven on the phone, see git history of the probe): CX GDSC, GX GDSC with resets and clamp,
+ * PLL0 ~532 MHz and the GX clock, GMU-wrapper clocks + SPTPRAC, GCC memory-path clocks, SMMU context bank 0,
+ * SQE microcode, ringbuffer, CP start, zap shader through the secure monitor, A2D blit.
+ */
